<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy seen offering 5.0 trln lire of Btps.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy seen offering 5.0 trln lire of Btps.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected to offer around 5.0 trillion lire of fixed rate government bonds (Btps) and 2.25 trillion of floating rate certificates (Ccts) at its mid-month auction, economists said.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters expected the quantity of Btps on offer would range between 3.5 and 6.0 trillion lire, while forecasts for Ccts ranged from 1.5 trillion to 3.0 trillion.</p>
<p>The Treasury will announce the quantity up for auction on Thursday and the auctions themselves will take place next week, on Tuesday for seven-year Ccts and 10-year Btps and Wednesday for three- and five-year paper.</p>
<p>Following is a table of analysts' forecast:</p>
<p>		   Btp 3-yr    Btp 5-yr   Btp 10-yr    Cct    TOT</p>
<p>Banca di Roma     2.0	   1.5	 1.0	  1.5     6.0</p>
<p>Bank of America   2.0	   2.0	 2.0	  2.5     8.5</p>
<p>Caboto		1.5	   1.5	 1.5	  2.0     6.5</p>
<p>Comit		 2.0	   2.0	 1.5	  2.5     8.0</p>
<p>Credit		1.5	   1.0/1.5   1.0/1.5    2.0   5.5/6.5</p>
<p>Indosuez	    2.0	   1.5	 1.5	  3.0     8.0</p>
<p>================================================================ CONSENSUS	   1.85	  1.6	 1.5	  2.25    7.0</p>
<p>--Milan bureau 00 39 2 66129507</p>
